NFS: Clean up O_DIRECT request allocation

jira KERNEL-814
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-4.18.0-553.117.1.el8_10
commit-author Trond Myklebust <trond.myklebust@hammerspace.com>
commit 70e9db69f927bb378db9aaa807cc83ae550779a9
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-4.18.0-553.117.1.el8_10/70e9db69.failed

Rather than adjusting the index+offset after the call to
nfs_create_request(), add a function nfs_page_create_from_page() that
takes an offset.

	Signed-off-by: Trond Myklebust <trond.myklebust@hammerspace.com>
	Signed-off-by: Anna Schumaker <Anna.Schumaker@Netapp.com>
(cherry picked from commit 70e9db69f927bb378db9aaa807cc83ae550779a9)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	fs/nfs/pagelist.c
#	include/linux/nfs_page.h
